# Citation metadata: GitHub reads this file to show the "Cite this repository" button.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Bluff Detector: Do Language Models Know They Don't Know Kenya?"
abstract: >-
  Hidden-state probes that detect when a small open language model is bluffing,
  measure the gap between what it internally registers and what it says
  (the verbalisation gap), and test whether fine-tuning breaks saying or knowing,
  on a natively authored Kenyan question set. Served as an answer-or-abstain
  FastAPI system with tracking, a model registry and CI/CD.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Trevor Anjeyo
    family-names: Vuhyah
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/trevorblue/bluff-detector"
keywords:
  - hallucination detection
  - uncertainty quantification
  - probing
  - abstention
  - selective prediction
  - QLoRA
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - MLOps
  - Kenya
